================================================================================
HOW map() UPDATES ONE ITEM
================================================================================

Suppose:

id = 'milk-1'


Array:

[
  Milk,
  Bread,
  Apples
]


map() processes:

Milk
 ↓
Does ID match?

YES
 ↓
Create NEW Milk object
 ↓
Toggle purchased


Bread
 ↓
Does ID match?

NO
 ↓
Return existing Bread


Apples
 ↓
Does ID match?

NO
 ↓
Return existing Apples


Result:

NEW ARRAY
│
├── NEW Milk
├── Bread
└── Apples


================================================================================
WHY USE THE FUNCTIONAL SETTER?
================================================================================

Use:

setGroceryItems(
  previousItems => ...
)


because the next array depends on the existing array.


This is preferable to:

setGroceryItems(
  groceryItems.map(...)
)


for this type of update.


MEMORY:

NEXT STATE DEPENDS ON PREVIOUS STATE
              ↓
        FUNCTIONAL SETTER


