================================================================================
CONTROLLED CHECKBOX
================================================================================

The critical code is:

<input
  type="checkbox"
  checked={
    item.purchased
  }
  onChange={
    handleCheckboxChange
  }
/>


Two responsibilities:

checked:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Reads the current value.


onChange:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Requests a change.


MEMORY:

checked
   ↓
STATE → UI


onChange
   ↓
UI → CALLBACK


================================================================================
DO NOT CREATE DUPLICATE CHECKBOX STATE
================================================================================

Avoid:

const [
  checked,
  setChecked
] = useState(false)


inside every GroceryItem when the actual value already exists as:

item.purchased


Otherwise there could be:

App purchased state

AND

GroceryItem checked state


These could become inconsistent.


Use:

checked={
  item.purchased
}


as the one source of truth.


