PART 8: COMMON ISSUES AND TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

ISSUE 1: CHECKBOX DOESN'T CHANGE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Check:

1. Is checked bound correctly?

2. Is onChange attached?

3. Is onToggleBought passed?

4. Is the ID correct?


Expected:

<input
  type="checkbox"
  checked={
    item.purchased
  }
  onChange={() =>
    onToggleBought(
      item.id
    )
  }
/>


================================================================================
ISSUE 2: onToggleBought IS NOT A FUNCTION
================================================================================

Possible problem:

GroceryItem expects:

onToggleBought


but parent passes:

onTogglePurchased


Example mismatch:

<GroceryItem
  onTogglePurchased={
    handler
  }
/>


Child:

onToggleBought(
  item.id
)


These are different prop names.


Choose one naming convention and use it consistently.


For this lesson:

onToggleBought


================================================================================
ISSUE 3: WRONG ITEM TOGGLES
================================================================================

Check:

• IDs are unique

• Correct ID passed

• Comparison is correct


Expected:

item.id === id


Debug:

console.log(
  'Received:',
  id
)


================================================================================
ISSUE 4: NOTHING MATCHES
================================================================================

Example:

item.id:

1


handler id:

'1'


Strict equality:

1 === '1'

=
false


This can happen if ID types are inconsistent.


Use a consistent ID type throughout the application.


Our newer items use:

crypto.randomUUID()


which produces string IDs.


Fixture IDs should ideally use a compatible identity strategy where
consistency matters.


