================================================================================
ISSUE 8: LOG SHOWS OLD VALUE AFTER setState
================================================================================

Problem:

setGroceryItems(
  ...
)

console.log(
  groceryItems
)


then the log seems old.


Reason:

The current function still has values from the render in which it was created,
while the state setter schedules/requests the next state.


Do not use an immediate old variable log as proof the update failed.


================================================================================
ISSUE 9: TOO MANY LOGS
================================================================================

Check whether logging exists:

• In JSX

• At the component function's top level

• In frequently rendering children


